From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350-b2q: disable ramoops

Its records never survived a reset on the Galaxy Z Flip3, and the kernel
console showed garbage at startup with it.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
index cfe6258..7346c79 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
@@ -239,12 +239,17 @@
 //			no-map;
 //		};
 
-		/* Samsung's own ramoops address on this board (stock base dtb). */
+		/*
+		 * Samsung's own ramoops address on this board (stock base dtb).
+		 * Disabled: its records never survived a reset on this phone, and
+		 * the kernel console showed garbage at startup with it.
+		 */
 		ramoops@f0b00000 {
 			compatible = "ramoops";
 			reg = <0 0xf0b00000 0 0x100000>;
 			record-size = <0x40000>;
 			console-size = <0x80000>;
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
 		framebuffer_internal: memory@e4000000 {
